Key observations:
- The element uses a 4x4 H matrix (shape function coefficients), inverted to get volume/shape derivatives
- G is the 6x6 material stress-strain matrix (isotropic)
- C matrices are 6x3 strain-displacement (B) matrices per node
- KIJ = C_i^T * G * C_j * HDETER gives the 3x3 block
- HDETER = |det(H)|/6 = volume

